course: dictionary
lesson: 815
title: The many faces of being
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word «being» can work in several ways, and the words around it tell you which one. In «you're being silly», being is a verb. It is the -ing form of be, and it shows how someone is acting right now. Look at the words after it to spot the meaning.
explain: In «human beings», being is a noun that means a living creature. The sentence is about people, so a being is a living thing. Ask yourself: what kind of thing is being talked about? If the answer is a living creature, you have found the right meaning.
explain: Sometimes «being» starts a phrase: «Being tired, he went to bed.» Here being tells you why he went to bed. «Being as it's raining, we'll stay in» is casual speech, so in your own writing say «because it's raining» instead.
explain: Use a swap test to check. Put a simple word into the sentence and see if it still makes sense. «Stop being a pain» can become «stop acting like a pain» and still work. When the swap fits, you have understood the context.
fact: «Being» can be a verb, the -ing form of be: «you're being silly» means you are acting silly right now.
fact: A «being» is a living creature, real or imagined: «human beings» and «beings from another planet».
fact: «Come into being» is a formal way to say that something starts to exist: «the chess club came into being».
fact: «Your being» means your whole self: «she loved him with all her being».
fact: «Being as» means because, but it is casual speech, so avoid it in good writing.
exercise: «Scientists are looking for other beings in space.» What is a being here? | A tool used in science | A kind of spacesuit | *A living creature, real or imagined | A planet with no air
exercise: «Being tired, he went to bed.» What does being do in this sentence? | It turns «went» into a question | It means he is a pain | *It starts a phrase that explains why he went to bed | It names a creature
exercise: «The chess club came into being when the new teacher arrived.» What does came into being mean? | Left the school | Went to sleep | *Started to exist | Was very loud
test: «Stop being a pain!» What does being show here? | Stiff, formal speech | *Behaviour that is annoying, right now | A kind of party | A living creature
test: «She loved him with all her being.» What does «all her being» mean? | Her shoes | Her little brother | *Her whole self | Her favourite song
exam: In «Being as it's raining, we'll stay in», what does being as mean, and why should you avoid it in good writing? | Staying in the rain, so it is a verb | Being wet, so it is formal | A living creature, so it is a noun | *Because, and it is casual speech
